1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,993
GTA 6 has the biggest cast Rockstar has

2
00:00:02,993 --> 00:00:05,985
ever built around a single story. So before

3
00:00:05,985 --> 00:00:08,978
you get lost in Leonida, here's who's who:

4
00:00:08,978 --> 00:00:11,971
the two leads, the people pulling their strings,

5
00:00:11,971 --> 00:00:14,963
and the details hidden in their backstories. And

6
00:00:14,963 --> 00:00:17,208
don't worry, this video is spoiler-free.

7
00:00:17,458 --> 00:00:20,251
Everything here comes from Rockstar's official character material

8
00:00:20,251 --> 00:00:23,045
and the setup you see in the first

9
00:00:23,045 --> 00:00:25,838
hours. No story twists, no endings. Just who

10
00:00:25,838 --> 00:00:28,282
these people are and why they matter.

11
00:00:28,532 --> 00:00:31,517
Let's start with Lucia Caminos. She's one of

12
00:00:31,517 --> 00:00:34,501
the two playable leads, and the first Latina

13
00:00:34,501 --> 00:00:36,740
protagonist in the history of GTA.

14
00:00:36,990 --> 00:00:39,550
Lucia's father trained her to fight from a

15
00:00:39,550 --> 00:00:42,110
young age. She ended up in Leonida Penitentiary

16
00:00:42,110 --> 00:00:44,670
after getting into trouble while defending her family,

17
00:00:44,670 --> 00:00:47,230
and she got out through a stroke of

18
00:00:47,230 --> 00:00:47,550
luck.

19
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:50,152
Now she's determined to turn her life around,

20
00:00:50,152 --> 00:00:52,504
and she's willing to bend the rules to

21
00:00:52,504 --> 00:00:54,856
take control of her future. Jason could be

22
00:00:54,856 --> 00:00:57,208
her route to a better life, or the

23
00:00:57,208 --> 00:00:58,384
thing that ruins it.

24
00:00:58,634 --> 00:01:01,421
There's even a link to older games. Lucia's

25
00:01:01,421 --> 00:01:04,207
official Rockstar profile says her mother wanted a

26
00:01:04,207 --> 00:01:06,994
good life for her ever since their days

27
00:01:06,994 --> 00:01:09,781
in Liberty City, the setting of GTA 3

28
00:01:09,781 --> 00:01:10,826
and GTA 4.

29
00:01:11,076 --> 00:01:13,812
Leonida Penitentiary isn't just backstory, by the way.

30
00:01:13,812 --> 00:01:16,548
It's a real location on the map, so

31
00:01:16,548 --> 00:01:19,284
you can visit the place that shaped her.

32
00:01:19,534 --> 00:01:22,103
The other lead is Jason Duval. He grew

33
00:01:22,103 --> 00:01:24,672
up around con artists and criminals, and he

34
00:01:24,672 --> 00:01:27,240
joined the US Army looking for a fresh

35
00:01:27,240 --> 00:01:28,846
start. He didn't find one.

36
00:01:29,096 --> 00:01:31,573
After the army, he ended up working for

37
00:01:31,573 --> 00:01:34,051
drug smugglers in the Leonida Keys. What he

38
00:01:34,051 --> 00:01:36,528
really wants is a quiet life. And the

39
00:01:36,528 --> 00:01:39,005
story keeps asking whether Lucia is the best

40
00:01:39,005 --> 00:01:41,482
or the worst thing that ever happened to

41
00:01:41,482 --> 00:01:41,792
him.

42
00:01:42,042 --> 00:01:44,538
You'll get to know Jason's world fast. He

43
00:01:44,538 --> 00:01:47,034
lives in the Keys, there are old photos

44
00:01:47,034 --> 00:01:49,530
hidden under the floorboards in his bedroom that

45
00:01:49,530 --> 00:01:52,026
fill in his backstory, and he even has

46
00:01:52,026 --> 00:01:53,586
a pet snake named Dolores.

47
00:01:53,836 --> 00:01:56,768
Jason's personal car at the start is a

48
00:01:56,768 --> 00:01:59,700
Vapid Ganado 70, a classic Ranchero-style pickup. It's

49
00:01:59,700 --> 00:02:02,632
not fast, but it says a lot about

50
00:02:02,632 --> 00:02:05,564
who he is: practical, a bit worn, and

51
00:02:05,564 --> 00:02:07,396
not trying to impress anyone.

52
00:02:07,646 --> 00:02:10,374
Together, Jason and Lucia are a Bonnie and

53
00:02:10,374 --> 00:02:13,101
Clyde-style duo. That's the heart of GTA 6:

54
00:02:13,101 --> 00:02:15,829
two people who might be good for each

55
00:02:15,829 --> 00:02:18,556
other, in a place that's terrible for both

56
00:02:18,556 --> 00:02:19,238
of them.

57
00:02:19,488 --> 00:02:22,432
Now the supporting cast, starting with Cal Hampton,

58
00:02:22,432 --> 00:02:25,376
Jason's friend. Rockstar's own line about him is:

59
00:02:25,376 --> 00:02:28,320
Cal is at the low tide of America

60
00:02:28,320 --> 00:02:29,424
and happy there.

61
00:02:29,674 --> 00:02:32,741
Cal prefers staying home, drinking beer and browsing

62
00:02:32,741 --> 00:02:35,808
the internet while listening in on Coast Guard

63
00:02:35,808 --> 00:02:38,876
communications. He believes the world is run by

64
00:02:38,876 --> 00:02:41,943
psychopaths and sees conspiracies everywhere. Jason has bigger

65
00:02:41,943 --> 00:02:45,010
plans, and Cal isn't sure he wants in.

66
00:02:45,260 --> 00:02:48,440
Then there's Brian Heder, a retired smuggler who

67
00:02:48,440 --> 00:02:51,619
still runs illegal operations from a marina and

68
00:02:51,619 --> 00:02:54,799
uses younger associates, like Jason, for the dangerous

69
00:02:54,799 --> 00:02:55,196
work.

70
00:02:55,446 --> 00:02:58,838
Brian worked the Florida coast during smuggling's most

71
00:02:58,838 --> 00:03:02,230
profitable era. His third wife, Lori, helps run

72
00:03:02,230 --> 00:03:05,622
the business. He looks laid-back, but Rockstar compares

73
00:03:05,622 --> 00:03:08,166
his business methods to a shark's.

74
00:03:08,416 --> 00:03:11,125
Next, Boobie Ike, described by Rockstar as a

75
00:03:11,125 --> 00:03:13,833
local Vice City legend. He's one of the

76
00:03:13,833 --> 00:03:16,542
rare few who turned street crime into a

77
00:03:16,542 --> 00:03:17,896
business that looks legitimate.

78
00:03:18,146 --> 00:03:21,026
His drug money financed property, a recording studio,

79
00:03:21,026 --> 00:03:23,906
and the Jack of Hearts strip club. And

80
00:03:23,906 --> 00:03:26,786
he co-runs the record label Only Raw Records

81
00:03:26,786 --> 00:03:28,226
with our next character.

82
00:03:28,476 --> 00:03:31,138
Dre'Quan Priest. He sold drugs to get by,

83
00:03:31,138 --> 00:03:33,799
but he always wanted a career in music.

84
00:03:33,799 --> 00:03:36,461
Now he runs Only Raw Records with Boobie

85
00:03:36,461 --> 00:03:38,124
and hunts for new talent.

86
00:03:38,374 --> 00:03:40,974
He organises performances at the Jack of Hearts,

87
00:03:40,974 --> 00:03:43,574
and he even uses the club's dancers as

88
00:03:43,574 --> 00:03:46,173
a test audience for new tracks. His own

89
00:03:46,173 --> 00:03:48,773
songs never took off, but he has a

90
00:03:48,773 --> 00:03:50,398
real talent for spotting talent.

91
00:03:50,648 --> 00:03:53,699
That talent is Real Dimez, the rap duo

92
00:03:53,699 --> 00:03:56,749
of Bae-Luxe and Roxy. They've been friends since

93
00:03:56,749 --> 00:03:57,512
secondary school.

94
00:03:57,762 --> 00:04:00,864
Before music, they extorted local drug dealers, and

95
00:04:00,864 --> 00:04:03,967
they used that experience in their tracks and

96
00:04:03,967 --> 00:04:07,069
their social media content. Their breakthrough single featured

97
00:04:07,069 --> 00:04:10,171
local rapper DWNPLY, and after five years of

98
00:04:10,171 --> 00:04:12,498
effort they signed to Only Raw.

99
00:04:12,748 --> 00:04:15,448
That makes the music business one of the

100
00:04:15,448 --> 00:04:18,149
threads tying this cast together: Boobie's money, Dre'Quan's

101
00:04:18,149 --> 00:04:20,849
ear, and Real Dimez's hunger. And all of

102
00:04:20,849 --> 00:04:23,212
it runs through the Jack of Hearts.

103
00:04:23,462 --> 00:04:26,508
And then there's Raul Bautista, a seasoned bank

104
00:04:26,508 --> 00:04:29,553
robber who recruits accomplices for big jobs. He's

105
00:04:29,553 --> 00:04:32,599
charming, cunning and drawn to high-risk work, and

106
00:04:32,599 --> 00:04:34,502
he turns down anything small-time.

107
00:04:34,752 --> 00:04:37,531
Raul is the one who pushes Lucia toward

108
00:04:37,531 --> 00:04:40,309
more professional crime. In Rockstar's gameplay footage, he

109
00:04:40,309 --> 00:04:43,088
helps Jason and Lucia escape the police during

110
00:04:43,088 --> 00:04:45,867
a heist. If you're here for the big

111
00:04:45,867 --> 00:04:47,256
scores, he's your guy.

112
00:04:47,506 --> 00:04:50,407
A couple more names to know. Andrés de

113
00:04:50,407 --> 00:04:53,307
León is a high-profile VIP that Jason and

114
00:04:53,307 --> 00:04:56,208
Lucia get hired to protect. Rockstar hasn't shared

115
00:04:56,208 --> 00:04:57,658
much about him yet.

116
00:04:57,908 --> 00:05:01,064
And Petra Navarro is the chief operating officer

117
00:05:01,064 --> 00:05:04,221
of Megamundo. She represents a completely different side

118
00:05:04,221 --> 00:05:07,377
of Vice City: corporate power instead of street

119
00:05:07,377 --> 00:05:07,772
crime.

120
00:05:08,022 --> 00:05:10,565
Beyond the main cast, you'll meet a set

121
00:05:10,565 --> 00:05:13,107
of contacts who matter for gameplay. In the

122
00:05:13,107 --> 00:05:15,650
Keys there's Kenton, who runs a scuba boat

123
00:05:15,650 --> 00:05:18,192
shop with a side business in underwater treasure

124
00:05:18,192 --> 00:05:18,510
diving.

125
00:05:18,760 --> 00:05:21,425
And Jason's neighbour Shirley has requests for you

126
00:05:21,425 --> 00:05:24,090
early on. Small, but it's part of why

127
00:05:24,090 --> 00:05:26,755
the Keys are worth exploring before you head

128
00:05:26,755 --> 00:05:27,088
north.

129
00:05:27,338 --> 00:05:30,224
In Port Gellhorn there's Moses, who deals in

130
00:05:30,224 --> 00:05:33,111
stolen cars and is where you register cars

131
00:05:33,111 --> 00:05:35,997
to keep them. Later, in western Vice City,

132
00:05:35,997 --> 00:05:38,162
Randy hands out high-end car contracts.

133
00:05:38,412 --> 00:05:41,175
And for loot, there are the fences. Yasmani

134
00:05:41,175 --> 00:05:43,937
in Little Cuba pays best for jewellery and

135
00:05:43,937 --> 00:05:46,700
marked bills, and Tyrone is the one for

136
00:05:46,700 --> 00:05:49,463
narcotics. None of them are main characters, but

137
00:05:49,463 --> 00:05:50,844
you'll see them constantly.

138
00:05:51,094 --> 00:05:54,015
What's left unknown is the good stuff: how

139
00:05:54,015 --> 00:05:56,936
these lives collide, who betrays who, and where

140
00:05:56,936 --> 00:05:59,857
Jason and Lucia end up. That's exactly what

141
00:05:59,857 --> 00:06:01,318
we're not spoiling here.

142
00:06:01,568 --> 00:06:04,234
So how does it all fit? Jason comes

143
00:06:04,234 --> 00:06:06,900
from the smuggling world of the Keys, through

144
00:06:06,900 --> 00:06:09,566
Brian and Cal. Lucia comes out of prison

145
00:06:09,566 --> 00:06:12,232
looking for a way up, and Raul offers

146
00:06:12,232 --> 00:06:13,232
the professional kind.

147
00:06:13,482 --> 00:06:16,434
Meanwhile Vice City's music and nightlife scene, Boobie,

148
00:06:16,434 --> 00:06:19,386
Dre'Quan and Real Dimez, sits at the centre

149
00:06:19,386 --> 00:06:22,338
of the city's money. And above all of

150
00:06:22,338 --> 00:06:25,290
them are the corporate players, like Petra Navarro.

151
00:06:25,540 --> 00:06:27,979
That's the theme Rockstar keeps returning to: everyone

152
00:06:27,979 --> 00:06:30,418
in Leonida is trying to climb, and most

153
00:06:30,418 --> 00:06:32,857
of them are willing to cross a line

154
00:06:32,857 --> 00:06:33,772
to do it.

155
00:06:34,022 --> 00:06:36,719
If you want my picks for who to

156
00:06:36,719 --> 00:06:39,416
watch: Raul, because every big heist in GTA

157
00:06:39,416 --> 00:06:42,113
history has needed someone reckless, and he's built

158
00:06:42,113 --> 00:06:44,810
for it. And Cal, because a conspiracy theorist

159
00:06:44,810 --> 00:06:47,507
listening to the Coast Guard always knows more

160
00:06:47,507 --> 00:06:48,518
than he should.

161
00:06:48,768 --> 00:06:51,572
And keep an eye on Real Dimez. Characters

162
00:06:51,572 --> 00:06:54,377
built around fame and social media usually end

163
00:06:54,377 --> 00:06:57,181
up at the centre of Rockstar's sharpest satire,

164
00:06:57,181 --> 00:06:59,985
and Vice City is the perfect stage for

165
00:06:59,985 --> 00:07:00,336
it.

166
00:07:00,586 --> 00:07:03,551
One gameplay detail that connects to the characters:

167
00:07:03,551 --> 00:07:06,517
Jason and Lucia each have their own criminal

168
00:07:06,517 --> 00:07:09,482
profile, and the one you're not controlling behaves

169
00:07:09,482 --> 00:07:10,594
according to theirs.

170
00:07:10,844 --> 00:07:13,135
So the way you play each of them

171
00:07:13,135 --> 00:07:15,426
shapes who they become. Keep Lucia professional and

172
00:07:15,426 --> 00:07:17,716
Jason violent, and you'll feel the difference in

173
00:07:17,716 --> 00:07:19,148
how they act around you.

174
00:07:19,398 --> 00:07:21,875
And this is where the duo really comes

175
00:07:21,875 --> 00:07:24,353
alive. For medium and high security robberies, you

176
00:07:24,353 --> 00:07:26,830
invite your partner from the map, and the

177
00:07:26,830 --> 00:07:28,998
two of them work the job together.

178
00:07:29,248 --> 00:07:31,970
Mid-job, you can pass stash bags from one

179
00:07:31,970 --> 00:07:34,692
to the other. Your partner sells the loot

180
00:07:34,692 --> 00:07:37,414
while you deal with the police. It turns

181
00:07:37,414 --> 00:07:40,136
the relationship into a real gameplay system, not

182
00:07:40,136 --> 00:07:40,816
just cutscenes.

183
00:07:41,066 --> 00:07:43,754
Even training is shared. If both of them

184
00:07:43,754 --> 00:07:46,442
work out at the gym, both benefit, no

185
00:07:46,442 --> 00:07:47,786
matter who you're controlling.

186
00:07:48,036 --> 00:07:50,509
But being a duo has a cost. The

187
00:07:50,509 --> 00:07:52,981
police track whether Jason and Lucia were seen

188
00:07:52,981 --> 00:07:55,454
together, and it shows up as its own

189
00:07:55,454 --> 00:07:57,926
icon. The fix is to split them up,

190
00:07:57,926 --> 00:08:00,399
which says a lot about the story's central

191
00:08:00,399 --> 00:08:00,708
tension.

192
00:08:00,958 --> 00:08:03,462
And you can switch between them, which is

193
00:08:03,462 --> 00:08:05,965
also the fastest way to travel, since the

194
00:08:05,965 --> 00:08:08,469
one you're not using usually waits near your

195
00:08:08,469 --> 00:08:08,782
safehouse.

196
00:08:09,032 --> 00:08:12,536
Quick recap. Lucia, the fighter fresh out of

197
00:08:12,536 --> 00:08:16,040
prison. Jason, the ex-soldier who wants a quiet

198
00:08:16,040 --> 00:08:19,544
life. Cal the conspiracy theorist, Brian the smuggler,

199
00:08:19,544 --> 00:08:23,048
Boobie and Dre'Quan's record label, Real Dimez, and

200
00:08:23,048 --> 00:08:24,800
Raul the bank robber.

201
00:08:25,050 --> 00:08:27,788
Who's your favourite character so far? Tell me

202
00:08:27,788 --> 00:08:30,526
in the comments. And subscribe, because next up

203
00:08:30,526 --> 00:08:33,263
is the new police system and exactly how

204
00:08:33,263 --> 00:08:34,290
to escape it.
